{number: 36}
{title: He Lives}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] I serve a risen Savior, He's in the world today;
I know that He is living, whatever [G7] men may say;
I [C] see His hand of mercy, I hear His voice of cheer,
And [D7] just the time I need Him He's [G7] always near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [C] lives, He lives, Christ Jesus lives today!
He [G7] walks with me and [C] talks with me a-[D7] long life's narrow [G7] way.
He [C] lives, He [C7] lives, sal-[F] vation to im-[A7] part!
You [D7] ask me how I know He lives?
He [C] lives with-[G7] in my [C] heart.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
In [C] all the world around me I see His loving care,
And though my heart grows weary I never [G7] will despair;
I [C] know that He is leading thro' all the stormy blast,
The [D7] day of His appearing will [G7] come at last.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Re-[C] joice, rejoice, O Christian, lift up your voice and sing
Eternal hallelujahs to Jesus [G7] Christ the King!
The [C] Hope of all who seek Him, the Help of all who find,
None [D7] other is so loving, so [G7] good and kind.
{end_of_verse}
